     ## Generating Manhattan Plots from GWAS Results                            
                                                                                
     The skill `plink-gwas` includes a dedicated R script that generates        
     both Manhattan and QQ plots from a PLINK `.assoc.linear` file.             
                                                                                
     ### The Script                                                             
     `/workspace/pigbole/.piggpa/skills/piggpa-G/plink-gwas/scripts/PLINK-G     
     WAS-linear-plot.R`                                                         
                                                                                
     ### Command to Run                                                         
     ```bash                                                                    
     conda activate R                                                           
     Rscript                                                                    
     /workspace/pigbole/.piggpa/skills/piggpa-G/plink-gwas/scripts/PLINK-GW     
     AS-linear-plot.R \                                                         
       --plink_assoc_file <YOUR_ASSOC_FILE>.assoc.linear \                      
       --output_prefix <PREFIX> \                                               
       --outdir output/                                                         
     ```                                                                        
                                                                                
     ### Required Input                                                         
     - `--plink_assoc_file`: Your PLINK association results (.assoc.linear      
     file)                                                                      
     - `--output_prefix`: Base name for output files                            
     - `--outdir`: Output directory (optional, default = current dir)           
                                                                                
     ### What It Produces                                                       
                                                                                
     | File | Description |                                                     
     |------|-------------|                                                     
     | `<prefix>_manhattan.pdf` / `.png` | Manhattan plot - SNPs arranged       
     by chromosome position (X) vs -log10(P) (Y) |                              
     | `<prefix>_qq.pdf` / `.png` | QQ plot - expected vs observed              
     -log10(P) |                                                                
     | `<prefix>_significant_snps.csv` | SNPs with P < 5e-8 (if any) |          
     | `<prefix>_suggestive_snps.csv` | SNPs with 5e-8 ≤ P < 1e-5 (if any)      
     |                                                                          
     | `<prefix>_summary.txt` / `_summary-zh.txt` | Summary stats (EN + ZH)     
     |                                                                          
                                                                                
     ### Manhattan Plot Details                                                 
     - **X-axis**: Chromosomes 1-N, SNPs ordered by base-pair position,         
     alternating colors per chromosome                                          
     - **Y-axis**: -log₁₀(P-value)                                              
     - **Horizontal lines**: Orange dashed at genome-wide significance          
     (P=5e-8, ~7.30 on Y), teal dotted at suggestive (P=1e-5, 5.0 on Y)         
     - **Title**: Includes genomic inflation factor (λ)                         
     - **What to check**: Peaks above the orange line = significant             
     associations; a single massive peak = possible major gene or artifact;     
     many isolated hits = possible population stratification                    
                                                                                
     ---                                                                        
                                                                                
